NAME
    ls - list directory contents

SYNOPSIS
    ls [PATH]
    ls --json [PATH]
    ls --advjson [PATH]

DESCRIPTION
    Lists the entries in PATH (default: current directory). Each
    entry appears on its own line. No -l (long format) flag for
    the bare mode; use --json or --advjson for structured output.

    --json    emits a single JSON object {path, entries: [...]}.
    --advjson emits JSONL (one record per entry, line-terminated).
              Activated automatically inside a `|>` pipeline; see
              docs/69-structured-pipelines.md.

    Each --advjson record has:
      name   16-char directory entry name
      type   "FILE" or "DIR" (computed from sys_fs_size; -1 = DIR)
      size   file size in bytes (omitted for dirs)
      perm   octal mode bits (e.g. 644)
      uid, gid

EXAMPLES
    ls
    ls /etc
    ls / |> where type=FILE |> count       # structured pipeline

EXIT STATUS
    0   listing emitted (even an empty dir is success)
    1   PATH does not exist or is not a directory

SEE ALSO
    find(1), pluck(1), where(1), count(1)
